                "Let us examine how to prepare an airtight STAR Story Bank: Elite candidates do not improvise STAR stories on the fly during an interview! Trying to recall a complex architectural conflict while your heart rate is elevated is a recipe for disaster. Senior engineers construct a 'Story Grid' containing 5 to 6 core crucible projects from their career. Each project is deconstructed into STAR format and mapped across multiple competencies: The same distributed migration project can answer 'Tell me about a technical challenge', 'Tell me about a time you disagreed with a colleague', or 'Tell me about a time you had to deliver under tight deadlines'. By mastering 6 versatile stories, you can confidently answer over 95% of all behavioral questions."
